  "description": "KCOV configuration for the A2 control-flow check. Witnesses are not listed here: each mirror decision (leanux-model --decisions) carries source spans for its outcomes, and the check intersects them with the lines that own a KCOV instrumentation point in these functions of the built kernel. 'files' bounds the source considered; 'functions' must include every function whose code (including inlined helpers) the modeled paths execute, and the check fails if coverage lands in a decision span the map does not know. 'known_gaps' lists C choice points KCOV observes but the mirror does not yet model; hits are reported, not failed. 'functions' scopes witnesses: only their PCs witness decisions, and a span line of an anchored C file covered by any other function fails the check; header helpers inlined into unlisted functions are not checked. 'branch_free_functions' lists C functions the compiler made branch-free (no KCOV point); only their decisions may lack an instrumented function.",
